                                        "entry_id": "fe9617c1-8249-3626-9a48-37157645bf04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A substituted benzimidazole (trademark Losec, Prilosec) which is a proton pump inhibitor and inhibits secretion of gastric acid, being given orally in the treatment of ulcers and gastroesophageal reflux; 5-methoxy-2-(4-methoxy-3,5-dimethyl-2-pyridylmethylsulfinyl)benzimidazole, C₁₇H₁₉N₃O₃S."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15019d50-ce29-42d1-bee1-f0d1d3797780",
                                                "sense_id": "7f3a6a72-7daa-3877-9a7b-78b9ae45fc53",
                                                "text": "2001: The first successful drug of this class was omeprazole (sold under the trade name Losec®), and it helped to change the medium-sized Swedish pharmaceutical company Astra, which discovered it, into a major player in the pharmaceutical industry. — Leslie Iversen, Drugs: A Very Short Introduction (Oxford 2001, p. 46)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
